Z||000000||Grasy||05-25-2000||08:52 AM||||I have an '86 Fiero GT with a 140,000 miles on it. I think it's um... time to defecate or get off the porcelain apparatus. <P>I'm not a gear head or a "do it yourselfer" so the information I learn here is helpful to me. However, I will trust my rebuild, if I get it done, to professional mechanics who drink beer while working on their own cars. <P>What I'm looking for is costs on a 2.8 in the "crate" and having that installed. Or, rebuilding my 2.8 . I realize that prices will vary from place to place. But a ball park figure from some of you will really let me know what I am looking at as far as expenses. Thanx in advance for posting yer reply.<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||pollock||05-25-2000||10:02 AM||||Welcome aboard.<P>GM offers a 3.4L V6 crate motor for about 1700.  It takes a few minor mods to fit it in a Fiero, but the block is the same size and will retain the Fiero fuel injection. This motor is intended as a replacement for 2.8L S-10 trucks, and in s-10 trim is rated at 160 hp and 190 ft-lbs. <P>There's a guy out in Alabama named Ed Parks.  His business is the Fiero Factory.  He's on the web and easy to find.  Ed is probably the authority on the 3.4L Fiero.  Check with him for pricing and details.||||reg||7
